# Issue RP-1 Create RepositoryPaths with its project and metadata roots

## Goal

Add the `RepositoryPaths` class. It stores the project root it is given and derives the `.minigit` root from it.

## Background

In HW8, `metadataDirectory(root)` took the root as an argument on every call. A class can store the root once, in a member variable, so later functions need no argument.

## Dependency

HW8 (PathLab Issues 1-4) merged.

## Functions to add

- `include/RepositoryPaths.hpp` and `src/RepositoryPaths.cpp`, in `namespace minigit`
- Member variables: `std::filesystem::path projectRoot_;` and `std::filesystem::path metadataRoot_;`
- `explicit RepositoryPaths(std::filesystem::path projectRoot);`
- `const std::filesystem::path& projectRoot() const;`
- `const std::filesystem::path& metadataRoot() const;`

## Acceptance criteria

- The constructor stores `projectRoot` and sets `metadataRoot_` to `projectRoot_ / ".minigit"`.
- Both getters return a `const` reference and change nothing.
- Nothing is created on disk.
- `CMakeLists.txt` adds `src/RepositoryPaths.cpp` to the `minigit_paths` library and registers a new `repository_paths_tests` executable with `add_test`.
- Local CTest and Windows/Ubuntu CI pass.

## Tests to write

For the roots `"course/repo"` and `"course/team/repo"`: `projectRoot()` equals the root, and `metadataRoot()` equals `root / ".minigit"`.

## Out of scope

`headFile()`, `indexFile()` or any other location.

## Reviewer focus

Is `.minigit` joined with `/`? Is the new test registered, so CTest reports two tests instead of one?
